      "content": "Do not take leftover steroids without a doctor's prescription, as they carry significant risks and can worsen certain conditions if used incorrectly. While vitamins might offer some support, you must see a healthcare provider within 24 to 72 hours to confirm the diagnosis and start effective treatment before permanent nerve damage occurs. Delaying professional care risks missing the optimal window for recovery, which usually happens in the first week for Bell's palsy. Please speak with your primary care physician or a local clinic today to discuss this safely.",
